      "writtenOn": "2020-12-08T08:09:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Irrespective of this code, I think moving of the oom_reaper_lock is unnecessary as the introduced flag, MMF_OOM_REAP_QUEUED, will now take care of avoiding the queuing same task twice to oom reaper. So, I will discard these changes in next patch.\n\nMy understanding about the TIF_MEMDIE is that it is solely used by the OOM path to indicate that a process is being terminated by the oom killer and accordingly managing the oom killed process. Eg: In the exit_mm()-\u003eexit_oom_victim(), we are decrementing the oom_victims and waking up all processes on oom_victims_wait, which are unnecessary for a ulmk killed processes.\n\nSetting TIF_MEMDIE also makes the process now to access to reserves, which may not be the problem here, but point to note.\n\nLet me know If you have other opinion here?",
      "parentUuid": "08dfa884_7e5c1b07",
